---
import '@fontsource/courier-prime/400.css';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../site';

const sections = [
  ['every-page', 'A library with every page'],
  ['small', 'A library small enough to count'],
  ['shuffled', 'Shuffled, not stored'],
  ['backwards', 'Running it backwards is search'],
  ['size', 'How big is it?'],
  ['wraps', 'It wraps around'],
  ['thanks', 'Prior art and thanks'],
] as const;

const symbols = [...'abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz ,.'];
const symbolName = (s: string) => (s === ' ' ? 'space' : s === ',' ? 'comma' : s === '.' ? 'full stop' : s);
const tinyPages = ['nnn', 'nno', 'non', 'noo', 'onn', 'ono', 'oon', 'ooo'];
---
<Base
  title="How it works"
  description="How one library can hold every page of 3,200 characters, and how your words are found in it: a shuffle that runs backwards."
>
  <header class="top">
    <a class="wordmark" href="/">{site.name}</a>
    <a class="back" href="/">Back to the library</a>
  </header>

  <div class="layout">
    <nav class="contents" aria-label="On this page">
      <ul>
        {sections.map(([id, title]) => <li><a href={`#${id}`}>{title}</a></li>)}
      </ul>
    </nav>

    <main class="column">
      <section id="every-page" class="hero" aria-labelledby="every-page-title">
        <h1 id="every-page-title">A library with every page</h1>
        <p class="lede">
          In 1941 Jorge Luis Borges imagined a library of hexagonal rooms whose books hold every possible
          arrangement of a few letters. Most of it is noise. Somewhere in it is everything ever written, and everything
          that ever will be.
        </p>
        <figure class="quote">
          <blockquote>
            <p>When it was proclaimed that the Library contained all books, the first impression was one of extravagant happiness.</p>
          </blockquote>
          <figcaption>Jorge Luis Borges, <cite>The Library of Babel</cite>, translated by James E. Irby</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <p>
          This library keeps his shape: four walls of five shelves in each hexagon, thirty-two books to a shelf, 410 pages
          to a book, 40 lines of 80 characters to a page. Borges gave his books 25 symbols. Mine have 29, all
          26 letters plus space, comma and full stop, so English can be found in them.
        </p>
        <figure class="symbols">
          <ol aria-label="The library's 29 symbols">
            {symbols.map((s) => (
              <li>
                <span class="glyph" aria-hidden="true">{s === ' ' ? '␣' : s}</span>
                <span class="visually-hidden">{symbolName(s)}</span>
              </li>
            ))}
          </ol>
        </figure>
        <p>
          A page is 3,200 characters, each one any of the 29. That makes 29<sup>3200</sup> different pages: a number
          4,680 digits long. Every one of them is on a shelf here, and none of them is stored anywhere.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="small" aria-labelledby="small-title">
        <h2 id="small-title">A library small enough to count</h2>
        <p>
          Shrink everything. Give the library two symbols, <span class="mono">n</span> and <span class="mono">o</span>,
          and pages three characters long. Now there are exactly eight pages, and the whole library fits on one shelf.
        </p>
        <figure class="fig fig-shelf" data-shelf>
          <div class="picker" role="group" aria-label="Choose a page, one letter at a time">
            {[0, 1, 2].map((i) => (
              <button class="tile" type="button" data-tile={i} aria-label={`Letter ${i + 1}: n`}>n</button>
            ))}
          </div>
          <ol class="shelf">
            {tinyPages.map((p, i) => (
              <li>
                <button class="book" type="button" data-book={i} aria-pressed={i === 0 ? 'true' : 'false'}>
                  <span class="label">{p}</span>
                  <span class="visually-hidden">, book {i + 1}</span>
                </button>
                <span class="place" aria-hidden="true">{i + 1}</span>
              </li>
            ))}
          </ol>
          <p class="readout" data-readout aria-live="polite">
            <span class="mono">nnn</span> is the first book. Read <span class="mono">n</span> as 0 and
            <span class="mono">o</span> as 1, and the page is 000 in binary: 0, the first place on the shelf.
          </p>
          <figcaption>Flip the letters, or take a book down. Each page is its own place on the shelf.</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <p>
          Finding a page here is counting. Read the page as a number, and the number is where it stands. The real
          library works the same way with 29 symbols instead of two, and 3,200 characters instead of three. The number
          is just very long.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="shuffled" aria-labelledby="shuffled-title">
        <h2 id="shuffled-title">Shuffled, not stored</h2>
        <p>
          Counting has a problem. Shelved in order, the first billion billion books all begin with the same 3,000-odd
          letter <span class="mono">a</span>s, and every book differs from the next in its last few characters. Borges's
          library looks like chaos from any shelf. So each place has to be shuffled into its page, by a shuffle that can
          be run backwards.
        </p>
        <p>
          I use a Feistel network. It cuts the page into two halves, mixes one half into a stream of noise, adds that noise
          to the other half letter by letter, and swaps them. One round barely disguises anything. Six rounds leave no
          trace of the order underneath, and because each step can be undone, every page still has exactly one place.
        </p>
        <figure class="fig plate" data-feistel>
          <div class="controls">
            <label class="range">
              <span>Rounds</span>
              <input type="range" min="0" max="6" step="1" value="0" data-rounds aria-describedby="rounds-value" />
              <output id="rounds-value" data-rounds-value>0</output>
            </label>
            <div class="stepper">
              <button type="button" class="pill" data-shift="-8" aria-label="Earlier places">Earlier</button>
              <button type="button" class="pill" data-shift="8" aria-label="Later places">Later</button>
            </div>
          </div>
          <table class="toy">
            <caption class="visually-hidden">Eight neighbouring places in a toy library of eight-character pages, and the page written at each</caption>
            <thead><tr><th scope="col">Place</th><th scope="col">Page</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody data-rows></tbody>
          </table>
          <p class="round-note" data-round-note aria-live="polite"></p>
          <figcaption>
            A toy page of eight characters: two halves of four. At zero rounds the page is just its place written in the
            alphabet. Add rounds and neighbours stop looking alike.
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
        <p>
          The obvious alternative is to multiply the place by a huge number and add another. That shuffles too, and it is
          easy to run backwards, but it leaves a tell. Neighbouring pages differ from each other in the same pattern,
          over and over: the stripes in the first panel below. The Feistel shuffle's differences are pure noise.
        </p>
        <figure class="fig plate" data-stripes>
          <div class="stripes">
            <div>
              <p class="panel-title">Multiply and add</p>
              <svg data-panel="affine" role="img" aria-label="Differences between neighbouring pages under multiply and add: the same pattern repeats down every row, forming vertical stripes"></svg>
            </div>
            <div>
              <p class="panel-title">Feistel, six rounds</p>
              <svg data-panel="feistel" role="img" aria-label="Differences between neighbouring pages under the Feistel shuffle: no pattern, only noise"></svg>
            </div>
          </div>
          <button type="button" class="pill" data-reroll>Compare other neighbours</button>
          <figcaption>
            Each row is the letter-by-letter difference between one real page and the next, first 48 characters. Measured
            over thousands of pages, multiply-and-add repeats the same difference at 66.7% of positions. The Feistel
            shuffle repeats at 3.46%, which is chance (1 in 29 is 3.45%).
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
      </section>

      <section id="backwards" aria-labelledby="backwards-title">
        <h2 id="backwards-title">Running it backwards is search</h2>
        <p>
          To find your words, the library doesn't look for them. It writes the page they're on, then asks where that page
          is shelved.
        </p>
        <figure class="fig plate" data-search>
          <label class="search-field">
            <span>Words to find</span>
            <input type="text" value="hello" maxlength="120" autocomplete="off" autocapitalize="none" spellcheck="false" data-words />
          </label>
          <ol class="steps">
            <li>
              <p>The library reads them as <q class="mono" data-read>hello</q></p>
            </li>
            <li>
              <p data-filler>It fills a page with random letters, seeded by your words themselves, and writes them in.</p>
              <pre class="facsimile" data-page aria-hidden="true"></pre>
            </li>
            <li>
              <p>It runs the six rounds backwards on that page. Out comes a place: a number up to 4,680 digits long.</p>
            </li>
            <li>
              <p data-address>That number is an address: a hexagon, a wall, a shelf, a volume and a page.</p>
              <a class="pill pill-solid" href="/#q=hello" data-walk>Walk there</a>
            </li>
          </ol>
          <figcaption>
            The same words always make the same page, so they are always in the same place. Ask for them elsewhere and the
            seed changes, giving another page that holds them too.
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
      </section>

      <section id="size" aria-labelledby="size-title">
        <h2 id="size-title">How big is it?</h2>
        <div class="powers" aria-hidden="true">
          <p><span class="big">10<sup>80</sup></span> atoms in the observable universe</p>
          <p><span class="big lit">10<sup>4680</sup></span> pages in the library</p>
        </div>
        <p class="visually-hidden">About 10 to the power 80 atoms in the observable universe, against about 10 to the power 4,680 pages in the library.</p>
        <p>
          Turn every atom in the observable universe into a universe of its own. Then do it again inside each of those,
          and again, fifty-eight levels deep. You still have fewer atoms than this library has pages.
        </p>
        <details class="fig number" data-number>
          <summary>Show the whole number</summary>
          <p class="digits" role="img" aria-label="All 4,680 digits of 29 to the power 3,200" data-digits></p>
        </details>
      </section>

      <section id="wraps" aria-labelledby="wraps-title">
        <h2 id="wraps-title">It wraps around</h2>
        <p>
          The hexagons are numbered in one long line. Each floor holds 2<sup>7764</sup> of them, a number 2,338 digits
          long, and stepping east moves you one number along. Walk east past the last gallery on a floor and you are on
          the first gallery of the floor above: the galleries are one enormous spiral. The stairs skip a whole floor at a
          time. After the last hexagon comes the first again.
        </p>
        <figure class="fig plate" data-spiral>
          <svg class="spiral" viewBox="0 0 340 250" role="img" aria-labelledby="spiral-place" data-map></svg>
          <div class="ways" role="group" aria-label="Move through the toy library">
            <button type="button" class="pill" data-go="west">West</button>
            <button type="button" class="pill" data-go="east">East</button>
            <button type="button" class="pill" data-go="up">Up</button>
            <button type="button" class="pill" data-go="down">Down</button>
          </div>
          <p class="readout-ink" id="spiral-place" data-spiral-place aria-live="polite">Hexagon 1: floor 1, gallery 1.</p>
          <figcaption>
            A toy library with five galleries a floor and eighteen hexagons. Arrow keys work too, once a button has focus.
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
        <p>
          The very last hexagon is nearly empty. 29<sup>3200</sup> pages don't divide evenly into hexagons of 262,400
          pages: there is exactly one left over. So the last hexagon has one book on its first shelf, and that book has one
          page.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="thanks" aria-labelledby="thanks-title">
        <h2 id="thanks-title">Prior art and thanks</h2>
        <p>
          The idea is Borges's, from <cite>The Library of Babel</cite>. The first library you could actually search is
          Jonathan Basile's <a href="https://libraryofbabel.info">libraryofbabel.info</a>, which holds every page of 3,200
          characters and finds text with an invertible random number generator. Reading how he did it is what made me
          want to build this.
        </p>
        <p>
          The two libraries are shelved differently. His shuffle is a linear congruential generator with extra mixing;
          mine is the Feistel network above, so the same words sit in different places in each. Mine is also a place,
          with galleries, stairs and lamps.
        </p>
        <p>
          I built this to make Borges's idea something you can walk through. Nothing is stored; every page is computed on
          your device.
        </p>
        <a class="cta" href="/">Find your page</a>
      </section>
    </main>
  </div>
</Base>

<script>
  import { explain } from '../explainer';
  explain();
</script>

<style>
  .top {
    display: flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: var(--space-2);
    padding: max(var(--space-2), env(safe-area-inset-top)) var(--gutter) 0;
  }

  .wordmark {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-variation-settings: 'SOFT' 100;
    font-size: var(--step-1);
    text-decoration: none;
    padding-block: 0.4rem;
  }

  .back {
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    color: var(--muted);
    padding-block: 0.7rem;
  }

  .layout {
    max-width: 78rem;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: var(--space-4) var(--gutter) var(--space-5);
  }

  .contents {
    display: none;
  }

  @media (min-width: 72rem) {
    .layout {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: 11rem minmax(0, 1fr);
      gap: var(--space-5);
    }

    .contents {
      display: block;
      position: sticky;
      top: var(--space-4);
      align-self: start;
      padding-top: 0.6rem;
      font-size: var(--step--1);
      line-height: 1.35;
    }

    .contents ul {
      margin: 0;
      padding: 0 0 0 var(--space-2);
      list-style: none;
      border-left: 1px solid rgb(185 138 94 / 0.45);
    }

    .contents a {
      display: block;
      padding: 0.45rem 0;
      color: var(--muted);
      text-decoration: none;
      transition: color 0.3s var(--ease-settle);
    }

    .contents a:hover,
    .contents a[aria-current] {
      color: var(--lamplight);
    }
  }

  /* text runs in a 40rem measure; figures break out to the right */
  .column {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: [text-start] minmax(0, 40rem) [text-end] minmax(0, 1fr) [wide-end];
  }

  .column > section {
    grid-column: text-start / wide-end;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: subgrid;
    row-gap: var(--space-3);
    padding-top: var(--space-5);
    scroll-margin-top: var(--space-3);
  }

  .column > section > * {
    grid-column: text;
  }

  .column > section > .fig,
  .column > section > .powers {
    grid-column: text-start / wide-end;
  }

  .column > .hero {
    padding-top: var(--space-3);
  }

  h1 {
    font-size: var(--step-display);
    font-weight: 380;
    line-height: 0.98;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    max-width: 14ch;
  }

  h2 {
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 1.5rem + 2.2vw, 3.2rem);
    max-width: 18ch;
  }

  .lede {
    font-size: var(--step-1);
    line-height: 1.45;
    color: var(--cream);
  }

  section p {
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  section .lede,
  .quote p {
    color: var(--cream);
  }

  .quote {
    margin: var(--space-2) 0;
    padding-left: var(--space-3);
    border-left: 2px solid var(--lamplight);
  }

  .quote blockquote {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .quote p {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-variation-settings: 'SOFT' 100;
    font-style: italic;
    font-size: var(--step-2);
    line-height: 1.22;
  }

  .quote figcaption {
    margin-top: var(--space-1);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  :global(.mono) {
    font-family: var(--font-page);
    font-size: 0.95em;
    color: var(--cream);
  }

  q:global(.mono) {
    quotes: '“' '”';
  }

  sup {
    font-size: 0.6em;
    line-height: 0;
  }

  .symbols {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .symbols ol {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.3rem;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
  }

  .glyph {
    display: grid;
    place-items: center;
    width: 2rem;
    height: 2.4rem;
    border-radius: 0.25rem;
    background: var(--parchment);
    color: var(--ink);
    font-family: var(--font-page);
    font-size: 1.15rem;
  }

  .symbols li:nth-last-child(-n + 3) .glyph {
    background: var(--lamplight);
  }

  .fig {
    margin: var(--space-2) 0;
  }

  .fig figcaption {
    margin-top: var(--space-2);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    line-height: 1.5;
    max-width: 40rem;
  }

  .plate {
    padding: var(--space-3);
    border-radius: var(--radius-card);
    background: var(--parchment);
    color: var(--ink);
    box-shadow: 0 24px 60px -24px rgb(0 0 0 / 0.6);
  }

  .plate figcaption,
  .plate p {
    color: var(--faded);
  }

  .plate :global(.mono) {
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .pill {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    min-height: 2.75rem;
    padding: 0 1.1rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--rust);
    border-radius: 999px;
    background: transparent;
    color: var(--rust);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    text-decoration: none;
    cursor: pointer;
    transition: background-color 0.2s, color 0.2s;
  }

  .pill:hover {
    background: rgb(138 59 38 / 0.08);
  }

  .pill:active {
    transform: translateY(1px);
  }

  .pill-solid {
    background: var(--rust);
    color: var(--parchment);
  }

  .pill-solid:hover {
    background: #75301e;
  }

  .plate :focus-visible {
    outline-color: var(--rust);
  }

  /* the eight-page shelf */
  .fig-shelf {
    padding: var(--space-4) var(--space-3) var(--space-3);
    border-radius: var(--radius-card);
    background:
      radial-gradient(ellipse 60% 70% at var(--lit-x, 7%) 30%, rgb(255 196 107 / 0.2), transparent 70%),
      var(--walnut);
  }

  .picker {
    display: flex;
    gap: var(--space-1);
  }

  .tile {
    width: 3.5rem;
    height: 4.2rem;
    border: 0;
    border-radius: 0.3rem;
    background: var(--parchment);
    color: var(--ink);
    font-family: var(--font-page);
    font-size: 2.2rem;
    line-height: 1;
    cursor: pointer;
    box-shadow: 0 3px 0 #c9b48f;
    transition: transform 0.15s var(--ease-settle), box-shadow 0.15s;
  }

  .tile:active {
    transform: translateY(3px);
    box-shadow: 0 0 0 #c9b48f;
  }

  .shelf {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(8, minmax(0, 1fr));
    align-items: end;
    gap: clamp(0.25rem, 1vw, 0.6rem);
    margin: var(--space-4) 0 0;
    padding: 0 clamp(0.25rem, 2vw, 1.5rem);
    list-style: none;
    border-bottom: 0.7rem solid #80492b;
    box-shadow: 0 1px 0 #a8673f;
  }

  .shelf li {
    position: relative;
    display: grid;
    justify-items: center;
  }

  .book {
    position: relative;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    width: min(100%, 4.4rem);
    min-width: 2.75rem;
    height: calc(var(--h) * clamp(8rem, 5.5rem + 6vw, 12rem));
    padding: 0;
    border: 0;
    border-radius: 0.35rem 0.35rem 0.15rem 0.15rem;
    background:
      linear-gradient(transparent 12%, rgb(0 0 0 / 0.14) 12% 15%, transparent 15% 85%, rgb(0 0 0 / 0.14) 85% 88%, transparent 88%),
      linear-gradient(90deg, rgb(255 255 255 / 0.12), transparent 30% 70%, rgb(0 0 0 / 0.18)),
      var(--spine);
    cursor: pointer;
    transition: transform 0.5s var(--ease-settle), box-shadow 0.5s var(--ease-settle);
  }

  .shelf li:nth-child(1) .book { --spine: #b84a33; --h: 0.92; }
  .shelf li:nth-child(2) .book { --spine: #d49440; --h: 1; }
  .shelf li:nth-child(3) .book { --spine: #4d736b; --h: 0.86; }
  .shelf li:nth-child(4) .book { --spine: #e8d1a3; --h: 0.97; }
  .shelf li:nth-child(5) .book { --spine: #7a4561; --h: 0.9; }
  .shelf li:nth-child(6) .book { --spine: #858c47; --h: 1; }
  .shelf li:nth-child(7) .book { --spine: #455480; --h: 0.88; }
  .shelf li:nth-child(8) .book { --spine: #cc7354; --h: 0.95; }

  .label {
    writing-mode: vertical-rl;
    padding: 0.5rem 0.15rem;
    border-radius: 0.15rem;
    background: var(--parchment);
    color: var(--ink);
    font-family: var(--font-page);
    font-size: clamp(0.9rem, 0.7rem + 0.8vw, 1.25rem);
    letter-spacing: 0.15em;
  }

  .book[aria-pressed='true'] {
    transform: translateY(-2.4rem);
    box-shadow:
      0 0 0 2px var(--lamplight),
      0 1.2rem 2.5rem -0.5rem rgb(255 196 107 / 0.55);
  }

  .book[aria-pressed='true'] .label {
    background: var(--lamplight);
  }

  .place {
    position: absolute;
    bottom: -2.3rem;
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  .readout {
    margin-top: var(--space-5);
    min-height: 3em;
    font-size: var(--step-0);
    color: var(--cream);
    max-width: 40rem;
  }

  .fig-shelf figcaption {
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  /* Feistel toy */
  .controls {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: var(--space-2);
  }

  .range {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--space-2);
    flex: 1 1 16rem;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-variation-settings: 'SOFT' 100;
    font-size: var(--step-1);
  }

  .range input {
    flex: 1;
    min-height: 2.75rem;
    accent-color: var(--rust);
  }

  .range output {
    min-width: 1ch;
    font-family: var(--font-page);
  }

  .stepper {
    display: flex;
    gap: var(--space-1);
  }

  .toy {
    width: 100%;
    margin-top: var(--space-3);
    border-collapse: collapse;
    font-family: var(--font-page);
    font-size: clamp(1rem, 0.8rem + 1vw, 1.45rem);
  }

  .toy th {
    padding-bottom: var(--space-1);
    font-family: var(--font-text);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    font-weight: 400;
